\details{
Wraps the ESPN core-v2 team awards endpoint
\code{sports.core.api.espn.com/v2/sports/football/leagues/college-football/seasons/{year}/teams/{team_id}/awards}.
The index endpoint returns a \verb{$ref} list of award resources; this wrapper
dereferences each one and returns a row per winning athlete for the
award. Athletes are returned as ESPN athlete ids (parsed from
\code{athlete_ref}); join to another athlete source for names. Most teams have
only one or two award items in a season.

When \code{team_detail = TRUE} (the default) the ESPN team catalog
(\code{\link[=espn_cfb_teams]{espn_cfb_teams()}}) is fetched once and friendly team fields are joined
onto every team-id column the output carries -- \code{team_id} and
\code{winner_team_id}. For each id column \code{X_id} the friendly siblings
\code{X_name}, \code{X_abbreviation}, \code{X_location}, \code{X_display_name},
\code{X_short_display_name}, \code{X_nickname}, \code{X_color}, \code{X_alternate_color},
\code{X_logo_href}, and \code{X_logo_dark_href} are inserted immediately after it.
A catalog failure degrades to \code{NA} rather than erroring the wrapper. Set
\code{team_detail = FALSE} to skip the catalog fetch and the join.
}
